## Step 6 — log the run and summarize

Insert one row into `scout_runs`, listing the sources you actually checked
(use the names `{{ scout_sources | join('`, `') }}`):

```sql
INSERT INTO scout_runs (
    terms_covered, sources_covered, candidates_reviewed,
    candidates_queued, candidates_from_backlog, cap_hit,
    candidates_overflow, notes
) VALUES (
    ARRAY['term1','term2', ...], ARRAY[{% for s in scout_sources %}'{{ s }}'{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}], 0,
    0, 0, false, 0, 'anything worth flagging'
);
```

Then report back in chat: how many new candidates were queued (and how many
came from backlog vs. fresh), a one-line list ({{ primary_label | lower }} —
{{ secondary_label | lower }}{% if artifact_enabled %} — {{ artifact_label | lower }} needed?{% endif %}), which sources ran and any that were
unavailable, whether the early-exit trigger or the hard cap fired, how many
postings got added to `reviewed_postings.jsonl` this run, and anything else
worth flagging (e.g. "criteria.md still has unfilled fields", "N candidates
skipped as probable duplicates"{% if uses_boards %}, "a company board couldn't be found"{% endif %}).

## The review loop (already built)

{{ queued_stage | tojson }} rows show up at `http://localhost:{{ port }}/queue.html` and
in the {{ entity_plural_label }} page's {{ queued_stage }} filter. From there
you open the source, act on it yourself, and click **{{ baseline_stage }}**
(flips the row to `{{ baseline_stage }}`, trigger logs stage history normally
from there) or **Dismiss** (flips it to `{{ closed_stages[0] }}`, which also
keeps it out of future dedup suggestions). Nothing in this skill needs to
know about that flow — it only ever creates `{{ queued_stage }}` rows.
